_struct_biol.id                    1 
_struct_biol.details               
;THE MOLECULE CONTAINS A CRYSTALLOGRAPHIC TW0-FOLD AXIS OF
SYMMETRY THROUGH THE CENTER OF THE 4-HELIX BUNDLE.  THIS
UNUSUAL ARRANGEMENT IS DUE TO THE SYNTHETIC NATURE OF THE
MOLECULE IN WHICH THE SAME SEQUENCE SEGMENTS REPEAT.  THE
SYMMETRY OPERATION REQUIRED TO GENERATE THE ENTIRE BUNDLE
IS (-Y+1, -X+1, 1/3-Z) AND IS GIVEN IN REMARK 350 AS AN
OPERATOR ON THE COORDINATES IN THIS ENTRY.
;
